1
00:02:30,059 --> 00:02:35,619
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:39,899
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,139 --> 00:02:44,119
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,699 --> 00:02:48,979
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,259 --> 00:02:51,739
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,139 --> 00:02:54,699
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,999 --> 00:02:57,839
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,839 --> 00:03:00,899
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,679 --> 00:03:04,059
This is exciting!

10
00:03:04,999 --> 00:03:07,679
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,179 --> 00:03:11,239
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,459 --> 00:03:15,439
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,359 --> 00:03:23,919
After losing his brother Ace, Luffy fell into despair.

14
00:03:23,919 --> 00:03:29,299
Weak! King of the Pirates!

15
00:03:29,759 --> 00:03:30,759
Dammit!

16
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:33,859
I'm too weak!

17
00:03:35,139 --> 00:03:37,299
However, after speaking with Luffy,

18
00:03:37,839 --> 00:03:40,599
Rayleigh convinced him to return to Marineford

19
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:42,779
and deliver a message to his crew.

20
00:03:42,779 --> 00:03:48,899
When the rest of the Straw Hats learned of his puzzling behavior

21
00:03:48,899 --> 00:03:50,519
through an article in the newspaper,

22
00:03:51,519 --> 00:03:54,779
they each found a new purpose in their journey.

23
00:03:56,699 --> 00:03:59,799
Because Luffy wants to become the King of the Pirates!

24
00:04:00,159 --> 00:04:01,239
And to help him,

25
00:04:01,499 --> 00:04:04,319
I need to be the best navigator the world has ever seen!

26
00:04:05,719 --> 00:04:06,899
Listen up, Luffy.

27
00:04:06,899 --> 00:04:10,219
The Thousand Sunny isn't giving up.

28
00:04:10,619 --> 00:04:11,219
Not ever.

29
00:04:12,339 --> 00:04:13,439
And as our captain,

30
00:04:13,819 --> 00:04:15,579
I know you aren't giving up either.

31
00:04:16,139 --> 00:04:17,599
So let's sail.

32
00:04:18,919 --> 00:04:19,519
Luffy,

33
00:04:20,039 --> 00:04:21,499
when we meet again,

34
00:04:23,499 --> 00:04:28,599
I'll be the best damn chef in all of the New World.

35
00:04:29,079 --> 00:04:31,879
I'll make food fit for the King of the Pirates.

36
00:04:31,879 --> 00:04:39,019
I will get much, much stronger!

37
00:04:39,379 --> 00:04:40,979
Zoros pledged to his captain!

38
00:04:43,799 --> 00:04:44,799
Antenagana Kingdom,

39
00:04:45,179 --> 00:04:46,699
on Sword Mountain Island.

40
00:04:48,239 --> 00:04:49,479
Ladies and gents,

41
00:04:49,699 --> 00:04:50,799
feast your eyes!

42
00:04:53,799 --> 00:04:55,739
What is everyone looking at?

43
00:04:55,819 --> 00:04:57,019
Must really be something.

44
00:04:57,459 --> 00:04:59,519
I heard they found some kind of crazy monster.

45
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:02,539
Come one, come all!

46
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:05,719
This is a spectacle you'll have to see to believe!

47
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:07,459
No organs!

48
00:05:08,179 --> 00:05:09,419
No skin!

49
00:05:09,999 --> 00:05:11,579
No eyeballs either!

50
00:05:12,159 --> 00:05:15,119
Step right up and meet the walking, talking skeleton!

51
00:05:16,219 --> 00:05:17,559
The strangest thing is,

52
00:05:17,599 --> 00:05:19,599
it's only got one set of elbows!

53
00:05:20,079 --> 00:05:22,639
Who knew such an anomaly could exist in this world?

54
00:05:22,979 --> 00:05:23,419
Hey!

55
00:05:23,719 --> 00:05:25,319
Do you think we're a bunch of suckers?

56
00:05:25,319 --> 00:05:26,519
Give me a break!

57
00:05:26,779 --> 00:05:26,999
Huh?

58
00:05:27,319 --> 00:05:28,939
Did we offend you?

59
00:05:29,519 --> 00:05:31,019
It's no walking or talking!

60
00:05:31,279 --> 00:05:32,499
I'm not paying for this!

61
00:05:32,659 --> 00:05:34,799
Yeah, it's just a stupid statue!

62
00:05:36,799 --> 00:05:40,739
It seems Luffy's made up his mind.

63
00:05:41,059 --> 00:05:42,419
There's no more time to waste,

64
00:05:42,559 --> 00:05:43,439
for me or anyone.

65
00:05:43,939 --> 00:05:45,099
Hey, Bonehead!

66
00:05:45,259 --> 00:05:46,299
What's the big idea?

67
00:05:46,819 --> 00:05:48,239
I'd better do something,

68
00:05:48,339 --> 00:05:49,019
and quickly.

69
00:05:49,859 --> 00:05:50,679
That's right!

70
00:05:51,099 --> 00:05:52,259
Sing, tap dance,

71
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:53,379
anything's fine!

72
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:55,539
We can't disappoint this whole damn crowd!

73
00:05:55,719 --> 00:05:58,019
But how can I possibly be of any use?

74
00:05:58,319 --> 00:06:00,759
He already told you that, lazy bones!

75
00:06:00,999 --> 00:06:02,719
Just get up and move around!

76
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:04,659
This is a rip-off!

77
00:06:04,659 --> 00:06:15,679
When he saw me for the first time,

78
00:06:15,779 --> 00:06:17,979
he wasn't afraid of my appearance in the slightest.

79
00:06:18,799 --> 00:06:21,299
He reached out to me without hesitation.

80
00:06:22,579 --> 00:06:23,859
Here's a question.

81
00:06:24,139 --> 00:06:24,599
You ready?

82
00:06:25,499 --> 00:06:27,219
Will you join our crew?

83
00:06:27,219 --> 00:06:29,139
Yes, certainly.

84
00:06:33,139 --> 00:06:34,759
I was overjoyed.

85
00:06:35,659 --> 00:06:37,079
For 50 years,

86
00:06:37,239 --> 00:06:38,759
I'd been drifting aimlessly

87
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:40,979
on those dark, lonely waters.

88
00:06:43,699 --> 00:06:45,399
My shadow was stolen.

89
00:06:47,479 --> 00:06:49,919
I don't want to hear you make excuses like that!

90
00:06:50,059 --> 00:06:51,819
If you need your shadow back so bad,

91
00:06:51,879 --> 00:06:52,999
then we'll get it back for you!

92
00:06:52,999 --> 00:07:21,119
I'm so glad to still be alive!

93
00:07:21,119 --> 00:07:25,759
Well, of course, right?

94
00:07:26,419 --> 00:07:29,139
Ah, so does the offer to join your crew still stand?

95
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:30,379
Yeah, welcome aboard!

96
00:07:30,679 --> 00:07:31,079
What?

97
00:07:31,799 --> 00:07:32,939
Just like that?

98
00:07:32,959 --> 00:07:33,879
That's real!

99
00:07:38,099 --> 00:07:40,599
You'll never know how much that meant to me.

100
00:07:42,819 --> 00:07:44,079
In that moment,

101
00:07:44,659 --> 00:07:47,039
I realized that my 50 years of waiting

102
00:07:47,039 --> 00:07:48,479
had finally paid off.

103
00:07:49,199 --> 00:07:50,219
Where's our money?

104
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:51,739
Yeah, give it back!

105
00:07:52,119 --> 00:07:52,439
Crap.

106
00:07:52,659 --> 00:07:54,959
Those stupid skeletons hanging us out to dry.

107
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:55,939
Find them.

108
00:07:56,539 --> 00:07:58,599
We'll just have to force them to get out.

