170
00:09:54,999 --> 00:09:56,219
We're sorry about that.

171
00:09:56,439 --> 00:09:58,739
We gave it our best, but you were hard to track down.

172
00:09:58,859 --> 00:10:00,199
What with changing crews and all.

173
00:10:01,319 --> 00:10:02,099
I'm teasing.

174
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:03,319
Don't you worry.

175
00:10:03,319 --> 00:10:06,239
In the end, everything worked out.

176
00:10:06,559 --> 00:10:07,919
And I don't have any regrets.

177
00:10:09,199 --> 00:10:10,359
Let's go!

178
00:10:10,699 --> 00:10:12,119
Time to head out to Baltigo!

179
00:10:12,119 --> 00:10:39,979
The sea's a vast place.

180
00:10:39,979 --> 00:10:43,059
Some day, you'll find friends who won't ever leave you.

181
00:10:46,719 --> 00:10:48,479
79 million berries?

182
00:10:48,819 --> 00:10:51,879
Why does an eight-year-old child have such a high bounty?

183
00:10:52,119 --> 00:10:53,819
They said she's one of the devils of Ohara.

184
00:10:54,299 --> 00:10:56,419
You know, those scholars who are plotting to end the world.

185
00:10:56,939 --> 00:10:57,419
Really?

186
00:10:58,419 --> 00:11:00,819
I heard she's saying six marine battleships, too.

187
00:11:01,239 --> 00:11:02,919
She must have some kind of weird power.

188
00:11:03,379 --> 00:11:05,139
Well, that explains the bounty.

189
00:11:05,139 --> 00:11:09,319
We can't let a child of the devil run wild.

190
00:11:13,479 --> 00:11:15,139
Okay, I'll be right over.

191
00:11:16,459 --> 00:11:18,799
Why did you come to save me in the first place?

192
00:11:18,939 --> 00:11:20,139
For the last time!

193
00:11:20,519 --> 00:11:22,159
I don't want you here!

194
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:29,739
Do you hear me?

195
00:11:30,239 --> 00:11:32,499
I just want to die!

196
00:11:34,079 --> 00:11:37,019
If that's Robin's enemy, then I know what to do.

197
00:11:38,339 --> 00:11:40,659
Shoot down that flag.

198
00:11:40,659 --> 00:11:50,519
No way!

199
00:11:50,719 --> 00:11:52,119
You're all going to die!

200
00:11:52,259 --> 00:11:56,019
You morons can't challenge the entire world and expect to win!

201
00:11:56,139 --> 00:11:56,459
Yeah?

202
00:11:56,699 --> 00:11:57,999
Bring it on!

203
00:12:02,999 --> 00:12:04,159
Robin!

204
00:12:05,619 --> 00:12:08,619
There's still something I want to hear you say!

205
00:12:08,619 --> 00:12:12,519
Tell me!

206
00:12:12,699 --> 00:12:14,459
You want to live!

207
00:12:21,959 --> 00:12:26,479
If I'm allowed to say my wish just this once,

208
00:12:27,099 --> 00:12:28,959
then I...

209
00:12:30,959 --> 00:12:33,939
I want to live!

210
00:12:35,459 --> 00:12:36,739
Take me with you!

211
00:12:36,739 --> 00:12:38,599
Take me away from here!

212
00:12:46,459 --> 00:12:47,259
Please, Robin.

213
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:48,459
Come back inside.

214
00:12:48,939 --> 00:12:50,319
You're going to catch cold out here.

215
00:12:50,999 --> 00:12:51,999
I'll stay here.

216
00:12:52,299 --> 00:12:52,779
Thank you.

217
00:12:53,499 --> 00:12:56,519
After all, I'm a pirate and you're revolutionaries.

218
00:12:56,999 --> 00:12:58,859
It's not wise to trust you yet.

219
00:12:59,619 --> 00:13:02,039
I can't go into a cabin without any exits.

220
00:13:02,899 --> 00:13:03,279
Robin!

221
00:13:03,279 --> 00:13:06,179
There's no reason any of us would ever want to hurt you.

222
00:13:06,599 --> 00:13:07,379
It's all right.

223
00:13:07,779 --> 00:13:10,239
This is the way I did things back when I was alone.

224
00:13:10,439 --> 00:13:11,279
Just let me stay.

225
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:12,579
Well, okay.

226
00:13:12,999 --> 00:13:13,879
If that's what you want.

227
00:13:14,119 --> 00:13:14,519
All right.

228
00:13:14,859 --> 00:13:16,599
Go get as many blankets as you can find.

229
00:13:16,999 --> 00:13:18,659
And get her some food and something hot to drink.

230
00:13:18,739 --> 00:13:19,419
Make it snappy.

231
00:13:19,759 --> 00:13:21,739
But we already set things up inside.

232
00:13:22,119 --> 00:13:22,659
Hurry up!

233
00:13:22,919 --> 00:13:24,699
And bring the sofa out here while you're at it.

234
00:13:24,959 --> 00:13:25,299
Sir.

235
00:13:25,299 --> 00:13:32,959
Luffy, do you think I can get stronger seeing the world through your father's eyes

236
00:13:32,959 --> 00:13:36,519
by walking in his footsteps until we meet again?

237
00:13:39,399 --> 00:13:43,019
This is the first time I've wanted to grow stronger for someone else.

238
00:13:43,819 --> 00:13:45,379
It's not such a bad feeling.

239
00:13:45,379 --> 00:14:04,739
Meanwhile, on the Bowen Islands on the Grand Line.

240
00:14:04,739 --> 00:14:11,359
What's gotten into you, Usoppin'?

241
00:14:11,359 --> 00:14:14,279
It's gotta turn all this fat into muscle.

242
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:16,819
Oh, that's a good idea.

243
00:14:17,099 --> 00:14:18,439
Gotta get strong!

244
00:14:18,759 --> 00:14:21,919
Because that's the only way to get off this island in?

245
00:14:22,459 --> 00:14:24,279
Gotta get really strong!

246
00:14:24,759 --> 00:14:26,539
Yes, you mentioned that.

247
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:28,799
Gotta get really, really strong!

248
00:14:28,799 --> 00:14:31,279
Uh, how strong, exactly?

249
00:14:31,539 --> 00:14:34,319
Really, really, really, really, really, really, really strong!

250
00:14:35,219 --> 00:14:36,959
You're quite serious, aren't you?

251
00:14:38,019 --> 00:14:39,939
But why the sudden change?

252
00:14:41,319 --> 00:14:43,799
What did you see in that newspaper and...

253
00:14:45,939 --> 00:14:52,619
Oh, Captain, sent us a message.

254
00:14:53,759 --> 00:14:54,239
Messaging?

255
00:14:55,439 --> 00:14:56,899
What are you talking about?

256
00:14:57,459 --> 00:14:58,279
Get on already.

257
00:14:58,799 --> 00:14:59,439
Huh?

258
00:15:01,179 --> 00:15:02,119
Come on!

259
00:15:02,339 --> 00:15:03,699
We're friends now, right?

260
00:15:14,699 --> 00:15:15,539
LUPI!

261
00:15:19,819 --> 00:15:21,059
Usopp...

262
00:15:21,059 --> 00:15:25,059
I didn't know you were here, too.

263
00:15:26,299 --> 00:15:27,119
Finish him!

264
00:15:27,119 --> 00:15:29,819
Then we can all leave this place together!

265
00:15:30,599 --> 00:15:32,599
I'll win no matter what!

266
00:15:35,859 --> 00:15:38,659
You know, I never doubted him.

267
00:15:39,019 --> 00:15:42,939
I just thought he could become king of the pirates with or without me.

268
00:15:43,379 --> 00:15:44,279
Of course he could.

269
00:15:44,279 --> 00:15:45,759
We're finally here!

270
00:15:45,759 --> 00:15:46,759
We're finally here!

271
00:15:46,759 --> 00:15:47,759
We made it!

272
00:15:47,759 --> 00:15:53,579
If we keep this up and sail around the rest of the world, we'll come to this wall one more

273
00:15:53,579 --> 00:15:54,019
time.

274
00:15:54,019 --> 00:15:57,819
And when we do, then I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

275
00:15:57,819 --> 00:15:59,299
But I was wrong.

276
00:15:59,299 --> 00:16:00,299
But I was wrong.

277
00:16:00,299 --> 00:16:04,299
Not because he's weak, but because others are strong.

278
00:16:04,299 --> 00:16:09,779
Even Luffy's not invincible, and he can't do everything on his own.

279
00:16:09,779 --> 00:16:15,539
So, I have to get stronger to protect him and the rest of the crew!

280
00:16:15,539 --> 00:16:21,019
Damn it, Heracles!

281
00:16:21,019 --> 00:16:23,279
I need your help, okay?

282
00:16:23,279 --> 00:16:26,919
Whatever it takes to improve myself, I'll do it!

283
00:16:26,919 --> 00:16:31,399
Please, Master Heracles.

284
00:16:31,399 --> 00:16:32,399
Huh?

285
00:16:32,399 --> 00:16:34,399
M-Masterin?

286
00:16:34,399 --> 00:16:35,399
That's right!

287
00:16:35,399 --> 00:16:37,899
You have weapons, so teach me!

288
00:16:37,899 --> 00:16:39,899
You're obviously a good fighter.

289
00:16:39,899 --> 00:16:43,899
If you can survive on an island like this, tell me your secrets!

290
00:16:43,899 --> 00:16:44,899
You...

291
00:16:44,899 --> 00:16:46,799
You really think I'm a good fighter-in?

292
00:16:46,799 --> 00:16:47,799
Sure!

293
00:16:47,799 --> 00:16:49,279
I mean, you're amazing!

294
00:16:49,279 --> 00:16:50,679
This is I!

295
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:52,039
Your Master-in!

296
00:16:52,039 --> 00:16:54,039
Heraclesin!

297
00:16:54,039 --> 00:16:57,039
I know that, but awesome!

298
00:16:57,039 --> 00:16:58,039
Uh...

299
00:16:58,039 --> 00:17:00,479
Please have a seat, Usoppin'.

300
00:17:00,479 --> 00:17:01,919
Yes, Master.

301
00:17:01,919 --> 00:17:04,979
Pay close attention, Pupilin'.

302
00:17:04,979 --> 00:17:08,659
This forest is full of plants called Pop-Greenzin'.

303
00:17:08,659 --> 00:17:12,019
They're known for turning hostile as soon as they sprout,

304
00:17:12,019 --> 00:17:14,059
which you've no doubt noticed.

305
00:17:14,059 --> 00:17:17,059
Now these are their Seedzin'.

306
00:17:17,059 --> 00:17:19,539
What do you use them for?

307
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:21,059
Many things.

308
00:17:21,059 --> 00:17:24,039
They each have unique applications.

309
00:17:24,039 --> 00:17:27,479
Hang in there, Luffy.

310
00:17:30,479 --> 00:17:32,479
Run, Usoppin'.

311
00:17:32,479 --> 00:17:34,979
This forest is your training ground, and...

312
00:17:34,979 --> 00:17:37,979
If it'll help you become king of the pirates,

313
00:17:37,979 --> 00:17:41,419
I'll become the sniper king for real!

314
00:17:41,419 --> 00:17:51,859
Meanwhile, on Gloom Island on the Grand Line,

315
00:17:51,859 --> 00:17:54,859
the ruins of Muggy Kingdom.

316
00:17:54,859 --> 00:17:55,859
Please!

317
00:17:55,859 --> 00:17:56,859
Please!

318
00:18:04,299 --> 00:18:07,299
Will you train me as a swordsman?

319
00:18:07,299 --> 00:18:08,739
You disappoint me.

320
00:18:08,739 --> 00:18:09,739
Stand up.

321
00:18:09,739 --> 00:18:15,739
I can't believe you would ask your enemy for instruction.

322
00:18:15,739 --> 00:18:18,179
Have you no shame?

323
00:18:18,179 --> 00:18:19,179
Get out of here.

324
00:18:19,179 --> 00:18:22,179
This is pathetic.

325
00:18:22,179 --> 00:18:26,179
A pity, perhaps, but I overestimated your worth.

326
00:18:26,179 --> 00:18:28,619
I said stand up.

327
00:18:28,619 --> 00:18:29,619
I said stand up.

328
00:18:29,619 --> 00:18:31,619
You're making a fool of yourself.

329
00:18:31,619 --> 00:18:33,059
I said stand up.

330
00:18:33,059 --> 00:18:34,059
Please!

331
00:18:34,059 --> 00:18:35,059
Help me!

332
00:18:35,059 --> 00:18:37,059
First of all, the baboons beat you.

333
00:18:37,059 --> 00:18:40,059
And after that, you couldn't even make it out to sea.

334
00:18:40,059 --> 00:18:41,059
I can't help you.

335
00:18:41,059 --> 00:18:42,059
I can't help you.

336
00:18:42,059 --> 00:18:43,059
It's hopeless.

337
00:18:46,499 --> 00:18:48,499
They didn't beat me.

338
00:18:48,499 --> 00:18:50,499
What?

339
00:18:50,499 --> 00:18:54,499
You're the only one left to take down.

340
00:18:54,499 --> 00:18:58,819
But, I'm just not good enough to win against you the way I am now.

341
00:18:58,819 --> 00:19:01,219
Anybody can see that.

342
00:19:01,219 --> 00:19:03,059
I don't follow.

343
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:05,859
Clearly, you still consider me your enemy.

344
00:19:05,859 --> 00:19:09,819
Yet, here you are, bowing down, begging for my help.

345
00:19:09,819 --> 00:19:13,059
What do you mean to do?

346
00:19:13,059 --> 00:19:14,059
Kill you.

347
00:19:14,059 --> 00:19:17,059
Of course.

348
00:19:22,939 --> 00:19:25,059
You admit you want to kill me.

349
00:19:25,059 --> 00:19:28,099
And you expect me to assist you in that.

350
00:19:28,099 --> 00:19:29,499
You're strange.

351
00:19:29,499 --> 00:19:31,439
What a ridiculous request.

352
00:19:31,439 --> 00:19:34,819
Aren't you the least bit embarrassed?

353
00:19:34,819 --> 00:19:39,819
Perhaps your priorities are different now, Ro-Ro-Noah.

354
00:19:39,819 --> 00:19:43,059
You, the ghost woman.

355
00:19:43,059 --> 00:19:44,819
Go take care of his injuries.

356
00:19:44,819 --> 00:19:46,419
Uh, what?

357
00:19:46,419 --> 00:19:49,219
Why on earth would I take orders from you?

358
00:19:49,219 --> 00:19:51,059
We'll begin after you recover.

359
00:19:51,059 --> 00:19:52,059
Huh?

360
00:19:52,059 --> 00:19:52,939
Huh?

361
00:19:52,939 --> 00:19:55,939
Mr. Fancy Pants treat me like some kind of maid?

362
00:19:55,939 --> 00:19:57,379
What are you waiting for?

363
00:19:57,379 --> 00:19:58,579
Let's go, stupid.

364
00:20:00,979 --> 00:20:02,579
He's a fool.

365
00:20:02,579 --> 00:20:06,819
But a man like that would not throw away his pride for his own sake.

366
00:20:06,819 --> 00:20:10,819
He must be thinking of someone else.

367
00:20:10,819 --> 00:20:14,499
3D is crossed out and 2Y is under it?

368
00:20:14,499 --> 00:20:15,819
You're right, I see.

369
00:20:15,819 --> 00:20:17,819
It's like a tattoo on his arm.

370
00:20:17,819 --> 00:20:23,059
A while back, the whole crew promised we would meet up in a certain place in three days.

371
00:20:23,059 --> 00:20:25,059
But we just couldn't.

372
00:20:25,059 --> 00:20:29,299
So let me guess, 3D means three days, right?

373
00:20:29,299 --> 00:20:33,299
Then, the 2Y is probably, um...

374
00:20:33,299 --> 00:20:34,299
Two years!

375
00:20:34,299 --> 00:20:35,299
I knew that!

376
00:20:35,299 --> 00:20:38,299
So the meeting is going to be two years later.

377
00:20:38,299 --> 00:20:39,299
All right.

378
00:20:39,299 --> 00:20:44,539
It means he pulled that stunt in Marineford, knowing it would get him in the newspaper.

379
00:20:44,539 --> 00:20:47,539
That way, he could make sure each of us got the message.

380
00:20:47,539 --> 00:20:51,699
That was smart, especially for Luffy.

381
00:20:51,699 --> 00:20:55,859
But none of us have what it takes to survive in the new world.

382
00:20:55,859 --> 00:20:58,499
That's why we have to train.

383
00:20:58,499 --> 00:21:01,139
So we'll all be stronger the next time we meet.

384
00:21:09,299 --> 00:21:10,299
Hey!

385
00:21:10,299 --> 00:21:12,299
Didn't I tell you to rest up?

386
00:21:24,299 --> 00:21:26,299
No way!

387
00:21:28,299 --> 00:21:30,299
See ya!

388
00:21:30,299 --> 00:21:32,299
You saved me?

389
00:21:32,299 --> 00:21:34,299
Who the hell are you anyway?

390
00:21:34,299 --> 00:21:37,299
My name's Monkey D. Luffy.

391
00:21:37,299 --> 00:21:39,299
I'm going to be King of the Pirates!

392
00:21:40,899 --> 00:21:48,299
Until the day comes when I defeat him and take his title, I swear that I will never lose.

393
00:21:48,299 --> 00:21:50,299
Is that okay?

394
00:21:50,299 --> 00:21:52,299
King of the Pirates?

395
00:21:58,299 --> 00:22:01,299
As long as I can still stand, I can train.

396
00:22:01,299 --> 00:22:03,299
Let's get started.

397
00:22:03,299 --> 00:22:10,299
There's one baboon you haven't beat yet.

398
00:22:10,299 --> 00:22:14,299
They've mastered swordsmanship by observing humans.

399
00:22:14,299 --> 00:22:18,299
They even organized by rank, all the way up to their master.

400
00:22:18,299 --> 00:22:22,299
He's the leader of every baboon on this island.

401
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:26,299
That sword.

402
00:22:26,299 --> 00:22:29,299
He learned to fight by copying what I do.

403
00:22:29,299 --> 00:22:31,299
He's not like the others.

404
00:22:31,299 --> 00:22:33,299
You should be cautious.

405
00:22:33,299 --> 00:22:35,299
Sounds like fun.

406
00:22:35,299 --> 00:22:38,299
You're nothing but a stepping stone, baboon.

407
00:22:38,299 --> 00:22:39,299
The 我更在看里面。

408
00:22:39,299 --> 00:22:58,299
The

409
00:22:58,299 --> 00:23:01,299
See you at Sub-Alone in two years!

410
00:23:10,219 --> 00:23:14,119
Plotting a course for his future, Luffy leaves Amazon Lily behind

411
00:23:14,119 --> 00:23:17,099
and travels with Rayleigh to the deserted island of Ruskaina.

412
00:23:17,579 --> 00:23:20,459
There, he struggles to unlock an arsenal of new abilities

413
00:23:20,459 --> 00:23:24,479
as he goes head-to-head against the giant creatures that inhabit the island.

414
00:23:25,039 --> 00:23:28,279
On the next One Piece, Luffy's training begins!

415
00:23:28,299 --> 00:23:30,839
To the place we promised in two years!

416
00:23:31,259 --> 00:23:33,019
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

